.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH CHGRP 1 "2026-09-01"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
chgrp \- Change the group of each FILE to GROUP.
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBchgrp\fR [OPTION]... GROUP FILE...
.br
\fBchgrp\fR [OPTION]... \-\-reference=RFILE FILE...
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Change the group of each FILE to GROUP.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Print help information.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-changes\fR
like verbose but report only when a change is made
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-silent\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
suppress most error messages
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
output a diagnostic for every file processed
.TP
\fB\-\-preserve\-root\fR
fail to operate recursively on \*(Aq/\*(Aq
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-preserve\-root\fR
do not treat \*(Aq/\*(Aq specially (the default)
.TP
\fB\-\-reference\fR \fI<RFILE>\fR
use RFILE\*(Aqs group rather than specifying GROUP values
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<GROUP>\fR
change the group only if its current group matches GROUP
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-recursive\fR
operate on files and directories recursively
.TP
\fB\-H\fR
if a command line argument is a symbolic link to a directory, traverse it
.TP
\fB\-L\fR
traverse every symbolic link to a directory encountered
.TP
\fB\-P\fR
do not traverse any symbolic links (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-dereference\fR
affect the referent of each symbolic link (this is the default), rather than the symbolic link itself
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-no\-dereference\fR
affect symbolic links instead of any referenced file (useful only on systems that can change the ownership of a symlink)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH "نسخه (VERSION)"
v(uutils coreutils) 0.11.0
